## 6. Per-function tests (TDD; red → green; one small commit per cycle)

`tools/exp10_yaw_pilot.py`
1. `waveform_gap`: identity → (0, 0); `rel_l2(w, 2w) = 1`; zero reference → finite; `[n, T]` → `[n]`.
2. `spectrogram_gap`: identity → 0; `logspec_mad` = mean|a − b|; `mag_rel_l2` uses `exp(out) − 1e-8` (checked against a hand computation).
3. `acoustic_gap` / `raw_measures`: identity → EDT 0, C50 0, T60 0; `want_t60=False` → NaN; all-zero input → NaN, no exception; canonical error == error rebuilt from raw measures where both finite.
4. `device_agnostic_apply_delay`: positive / negative / zero delays on CPU; equals `model.xRIR.apply_delay` on CUDA when available (skip otherwise); `patched_apply_delay` restores the original, also when the block raises.
5. `angle_logspec` (random-init `build_xrir("simple", 2)`, synthetic batch, CPU): k = 0 equals the plain forward exactly; **k = 128 equals the trusted composition** `rotate_scene_yaw` + `fixed_alignment` + `model(...)` written out in the test; reference and target audio are unchanged by the call; `shift_and_align` is not called inside the pinned block (counter); angle-order invariance (ks in two orders → identical outputs); restoration after an exception inside the block.
6. `invert`: same `(out, key, gl_seed)` twice → identical; different key → different; `[n, 9600]` float32, last 21 samples zero; the returned array is the one the metrics consume (no clipping/normalisation).
7. `evaluate_batch`: batch of 3 padded to 4 → n = 3; both metric families + raw measures at every k; k = 0 gaps exactly 0; kept rows identical whether the 3 queries are alone or inside a batch of 4; controls with distinct ids run **fresh inference** (call counter increases).
8. `select_probe_batches`: on a synthetic manifest with contiguous rooms returns one intact batch per room, each entirely inside its room; refuses rooms with no full batch.
9. `run` smoke (`--batches 0`, real manifest, CPU; skipped without data): outputs and meta complete (all §5 fields, array sha256s match, `complete` true); refuses a wrong `--manifest-hash` and a K mismatch; a second run is bit-identical on CPU; save/load round trip of `wav_k*.npy` is exact.

`tools/exp10_compare.py`
10. Offline Metric 1 == online (1e-6); meta guard refuses different gl_seed / manifest / checkpoint sha / K / array sha / `complete = false`.
11. `parity_exp03`: accepts a valid non-contiguous probe subset (rows extracted by canonical index, ordered equality); refuses a different manifest hash, and missing / duplicate / reordered queries; on a fixture with an injected per-sample offset reports max |Δ|, mean |Δ|, paired-Δ difference, sign agreement and validity-mask mismatches exactly. `verify_exp03_pins`: passes on the untouched tree; fails on a fixture whose one file is altered; the comparison is written into meta by `run`.

`tools/exp10_summarize.py`
12. Bootstrap contract: one shared draw per replicate (Δ*, G*, R* from the same indices — checked by injecting a query whose exclusion changes all three); shared mask excludes a query invalid in any of `e_0`, `e_α`, `g_α`; exclusion counts by cause; seeded reproducibility; synthetic shift recovered inside the CI; status `defined` / `improvement` / `denominator uncertain` / `undefined` each hit by a fixture (including exact-zero draws counted, not dropped); empty mask → reported as n = 0 with no interval, no exception.
13. Room-cluster bootstrap: drawn-room multiplicities preserved and query-weighted (a fixture with unequal room sizes where per-room averaging would give a different answer).
14. Controls table: flags `ctrl_full_turn` / `ctrl_zero_repeat` / `ctrl_k128_repeat` mismatches > 1e-6 (waveform and log-spec) and > 1e-9 on acoustic metrics.
